    18	
    19	# Design — development-document-level project-memory standard
    20	
    21	## Problem
    22	
    23	PR #272 fixed where memory files live and what they are named. It did NOT define or enforce
    24	how well each doc is written as a development document. Two evidenced consequences (HEAD d2b5b37):
    25	1. Frontmatter never retrofitted: 50 / 208 live docs carry the full base schema (~24%).
    26	2. Cryptic session-internal references survive in doc bodies (confirmed at
    27	   `features/git-workflow/design/worktree-create-before-session-stamp.md:31-33,49-51`).
    28	
    29	## Scope
    30	
    31	**In-scope (three tiers, priority order):**
    32	- Tier 1 (primary): write the dev-doc standard as a new section in `memorization/rules.md`;
    33	  run conformance wave (mechanical, type-aware FIX-1 strip + base-schema normalization);
    34	  run prose-quality wave (per-type rewrite).
    35	- Tier 2 (optional): minimal mechanical grep gate extended to `features/` (verification
    36	  command only; no behavioral change; heavier enforcement deferred).
    37	- Tier 3 (tertiary): light nav wave — verify each feature README.md's Subdirectories section.
    38	
    39	**Out-of-scope:** re-home, big-bang rewrite, new eval perspective, Principle-13 surgery,
    40	frozen archive/ docs, stripping legitimate per-type frontmatter keys.
    41	
    42	## Approach
    43	
    44	### Standard authoring (wave 0 — the spec)
    45	A new section is added to `memorization/rules.md` (canonical:
    46	`.gobbi/projects/gobbi/skills/memorization/rules.md`). The section:
    47	- Defines a dev-doc (a doc a zero-context reader understands end-to-end).
    48	- Leads with "what good looks like" + a real before/after table drawn from this tree.
    49	- Specifies per-type section contracts:
    50	  - decisions/design → Context → Decision → Rationale → Alternatives → Consequences → Related (ADR-shaped).
    51	  - mistakes → What/Why/Recognize/Corrected (existing enforced schema).
    52	  - learnings → Insight → Context → Why-it-matters → How-to-apply → Counter-cases.
    53	  - notes → What-happened → What-shipped → Deferred → Decisions-to-respect.
    54	- States the self-contained-prose rule: no load-bearing vanished-session coordinates in bodies.
    55	- States the type-purity rule (per Diátaxis): one doc, one type's job; do not blend types.
    56	
    57	### Conformance wave (wave 1 — mechanical)
    58	Apply the FIX-1 type-aware allowlist strip (see [type-aware-strip-disposition-not-blanket-leak](../decisions/type-aware-strip-disposition-not-blanket-leak.md) for the full predicate).
    59	Also normalize base schema (add missing base keys) and de-crypt cryptic session-coord body
    60	references. Absorb backlog `feature-dir-frontmatter-full-normalization.md`.
    61	
    62	### Prose-quality wave (wave 2 — per type)
    63	Rewrite bodies toward the quality bar, type-by-type. Verify per wave.
    64	
    65	### Tier-3 nav wave (wave 3 — light, lowest priority)
    66	Verify each feature README.md's Subdirectories section; optionally add top-level index pointer.
    67	Must not block tier-1.
    68	
    69	## Scenarios
    70	
    71	- **Golden path:** a new `decisions/` doc authored next session passes type-purity + ADR section
    72	  contract + base frontmatter + self-contained-prose checks with zero rework.
    73	- **Edge (legitimate-key backlog):** a `backlogs/` doc with both legitimate `disposition` AND
    74	  illegitimate eval-routing keys — FIX-1 predicate strips the eval keys, preserves `disposition`.
    75	- **Edge (half-narrative):** a migrated design doc with `T1-I-2` / `draft-iter3.md:308` in the
    76	  body — retrofit keeps the decision prose, lifts provenance to frontmatter/footer, drops inline
    77	  coordinates.
    78	- **Failure (no clear home):** a session-journal mislabeled as `design/` — reclassify to `notes/`;
    79	  never delete.
    80	
    81	## Validation
    82	
    83	- Standard section exists in canonical `rules.md`; symlink auto-reflects.
    84	- Conformance wave: type-aware grep gate reports 0 illegitimate keys; 100% P_live_all (208) carry
    85	  base schema.
    86	- Prose wave: evaluator scores 3 sample docs against the section-contract checklist — pass/fail.
    87	- Nav wave: each feature README.md Subdirectories section lists all existing subdirs.
    88	
    89	## Trade-offs
    90	
    91	- Optimizes for: durable, machine-addressable project memory that a zero-context reader can
    92	  navigate without re-reading session transcripts.
    93	- Sacrifices: one-shot speed (wave-based is slower than big-bang, but de-risked per Principle 3).
    94	- Wave-based approach honors the steel-man's anti-big-bang warning while staying bottom-up.
    95	
    96	## Open issues
    97	
    98	- **CN-1 (Low, cosmetic):** FIX-1 disposition sub-count cross-foot (28 vs 27 under strict filter).
    99	  Normalize at Execution.
   100	- **PR-1 (Low, confirm/defer):** AGENTS.md 12→13 entrypoint reconciliation — surface at Planning.
   101	- **12/13/16 type-count framing:** when authoring the standard's per-type section list, reconcile
   102	  against `rules.md` §2 (12 promotable + 4 feature-subdir-only = 16) and `memory-map.md` (13 types).
   103	  Not a blocker; a standard-authoring concern for Execution.

