    16	
    17	# Memorization moment-of-capture Core Principle
    18	
    19	## Problem
    20	
    21	The write-as-you-go discipline gap lives in WORK: corrections, decisions, and mistake-candidates that surface during a loop's DISCUSSION are often deferred to the MEMORIZATION sub-phase and then silently lost when a session is interrupted. The corrective documentation, however, lives in MEMORIZATION's contract, so the discipline needs a home that every agent loading memorization will see.
    22	
    23	## Scope
    24	
    25	In-scope: add one Core Principle bullet to the memorization skill and a reciprocal link to the mistake skill's P2. Out-of-scope: changing the MEMORIZATION procedure steps or the staging routing.
    26	
    27	## Approach
    28	
    29	Add a new Core Principle bullet, "Moment-of-capture, not end-of-loop," to the memorization skill's Core Principles section — placed after "Store what survives, not what's transient" and before "Templates over freeform." The body states in two or three sentences that corrections / decisions / mistake-candidates are written to staging or rawdata at the moment of occurrence during WORK, not deferred to MEMORIZATION. Add a reciprocal link to the mistake skill's P2, which already says "Do not defer to MEMORIZATION" — the two-way link closes the loop between the two skills.
    30	
    31	## Validation
    32	
    33	- `grep -i "moment-of-capture" memorization/SKILL.md` returns at least one match.
    34	- `grep "memorization/SKILL.md" mistake/SKILL.md` returns the reciprocal link.
    35	
    36	## Trade-offs
    37	
    38	Optimizes for visibility (the discipline appears wherever memorization is loaded) at the cost of a small duplication of intent between the memorization Core Principle and the mistake skill's P2 — accepted because the reciprocal link keeps them in sync.
    39	
    40	## Open issues
    41	
    42	None — the principle and the reciprocal link are both additive.
    43	
    44	## Related
    45	
    46	- [`skills/memorization/SKILL.md`](../../../skills/memorization/SKILL.md) — the skill the Core Principle bullet was added to
    47	- [`skills/mistake/SKILL.md`](../../../skills/mistake/SKILL.md) — the P2 the new bullet reciprocally links to

